  "text": "When the pandemic hit, the gambling world was in shock. Most sports events were cancelled, so the Russian casino lords thought to themselves, how do we provide those peasants with live sports games to bet on? Introducing Sports Betting Farms. They hired regular people, put them in a closed court, assigned them to made-up teams, and just gave them a ball. Hundreds of these short games were being streamed at once, and once someone scored, no one cared. Because they weren't paid to be good players, they were paid to just generate an event. something for those gambling addicts to bet on. Now this is still happening to this day, and these shady companies are known for providing their players with low pay and grueling work hours. This makes for probably the least enthusiastic gameplay I've ever seen from what are I guess, technically professional players, you know, cause they're getting paid to play and are being broadcast, even though you can sometimes literally see the same person playing different sports."
